I did this once, but in Larn. Going on the mistaken
impression that the dungeon levels were algorithmic,
I developed algorithms (in C, IIRC) that laid out
the same kind of dungeon levels. Only later, with
access to the game source, did I discover that each
level was fixed, and laid out by the game author by
hand, not by algorithm.

I was in the end even happier that my algorithms
matched the results of a human designer's work.

